The overshoot that will not go away

Add harmonics to a square wave and the partial sum gets closer everywhere
except at the jump, where it always shoots about 9% too far. More terms
make the overshoot narrower, never shorter.

 harmonics      peak value       overshoot
--------------------------------------------
         3       1.2004218        10.0211%
         5       1.1883566         9.4178%
        11       1.1813016         9.0651%
        21       1.1796688         8.9834%
        51       1.1791028         8.9551%
       101       1.1790115         8.9506%
       201       1.1789877         8.9494%
       401       1.1789816         8.9491%
--------------------------------------------
     limit       1.1789797         8.9490%

The limit is 2*Si(pi)/pi, where Si is the sine integral -- computed
here by the same midpoint rule, not looked up.
